= gone_simultaneous

// BEAT: Both mechanisms failing at once.
// Dale can still see Val — high suspicion kept Val solid in his perception
// even as erasure thinned them out. He steps forward to act on it.
// His hand passes through Val's shoulder.
// Neither mechanism completes. Neither needed to.
// Key image: "Two mechanisms failing in parallel."
// The space where Val was smooths over.

-> gone_shared


= gone_dale

// BEAT: Dale acts first.
// Not the looping clipboard version from the parking lot — a different configuration:
// mining jumpsuit, 1973, hands empty. He was waiting.
// dale_suspicion level flavors the beat:
//   >= 9: Val found a lot (records, passage, library). System was thorough in return.
//   == 8: one threshold moment too many.
// Three steps. Grip closes. Mine closes. Not violent — administrative.
// Corridor was here. Then wasn't. Dale returns to the desk. Loops.

-> gone_shared


= gone_erasure

// BEAT: Val is already gone before anything acts on them.
// Nobody at check-in. Val walks to Zone 2 on muscle memory.
// Gets in the boo hole. Does the job — hits the window, screams, exactly right.
// The group doesn't react. Eyes slide past. Nobody receives the scare.
// Val steps into the corridor. One foot away. Eyes slide past.
// The mine didn't do anything. It just waited for Val to get thin enough.
// "Thin enough is the same as not there."

-> gone_shared


= gone_portal

// BEAT: Val steps into the portal without ritual, without protection, without a map.
// Not dissolution — not thinning out over days. A single decisive moment.
// No ritual knowledge, no containment circuit, no guide. Just the edge and the step.
// The amber light doesn't feel like light. The hum doesn't feel like sound.
// The Figure watched. Didn't stop them. Didn't follow.
// The other side receives Val the way stone receives water: completely, without remainder.

-> gone_shared


= gone_shared

